Z||000015||Leadfoot||07-13-2001||10:21 AM||||Mach10 just put in a new boot.  It's really not that hard to do.  It'll take an hour at the most.  Driving without a boot will eventually allow the dirt and dust to work it's way into the joint.  How long it will last depends on the envirionment you drive in and your driving habits.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Leadfoot||07-13-2001||10:24 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>G has a question   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>How mucch should one pay for upper & lower balljoints for a 88?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>About $60 bucks at the fiero store.  However, check your local autoparts store, they might have them for less.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||KissMySSFiero||07-13-2001||07:39 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Galen:<BR><B>G has a question   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>How mucch should one pay for upper & lower balljoints for a 88?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>i payed $60 each for the uppers from the fiero store plus %10 discount for being in a fiero club.  i found lowers for about $30-35 at autozone.<P>------------------<BR>JOEJOE Aol:SSFiero <P>88FORMULA<BR>      <A HREF="mailto:SSFiero@Aol.com">SSFiero@Aol.com</A>       <P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FORUMSIG1.jpg">           <BR>"Kids in the backseat cause accidents,  accidents in the backseat caused me!!"||||reg||1
Z||000018||shawnster||07-14-2001||07:08 PM||||I have to do a lower ball joint on the front too and I bought a Haynes Manual and it says the lower ball joint is welded to the control arm and cannot be replaced..anyone out there have this problem? Oh..Its an 84 if that makes a difference..<P>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Oreif||07-14-2001||11:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by shawnster:<BR><B>I have to do a lower ball joint on the front too and I bought a Haynes Manual and it says the lower ball joint is welded to the control arm and cannot be replaced..anyone out there have this problem? Oh..Its an 84 if that makes a difference..<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>You can grind the welds, press out the old then press in the new. All 84 thru 87 have them tac-welded. When I changed mine we used a dremel to carefully grind the weld. You can tac-weld the new ones in if you want but the MOOG's have a safety clip and if pressed correctly won't come loose.<BR>||||reg||1
